{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938598-evan-heals-the-past-a-mary-sue","id":938598,"title":"Evan Heals the Past, a Mary sue?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-27T22:07:01-07:00","id":938598,"title":"Evan Heals the Past, a Mary sue?","content":"I'd agree he isnt as horrible Sam Haight wound up becoming, but he is an almost oxymoronic charachter arising from a freak accident (a rape over a century ago) <br /> <br /> I read the &quot;Legends of the Garou&quot; in the 2nd Edition Players guide and saw how he was acosted and accused of being a white boy driven to tears by movies, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> is it safe to say that many even after divinations confirm the legitimacy of his bloodline, suggested he'd be better off elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T22:19:11-07:00","id":938608,"title":"","content":"No more then Albrecht or really any other npc's really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:05:20-07:00","id":938624,"title":"","content":"Evan isn't a Mary Sue by the classic definition as such. A Mary Sue's character flaws are really non-flaws that only serve to make other characters like them more in the long run. Evan's story actually has him have to work to overcome prejudice on both sides of his main issue. As well, he's advanced significantly by Albrecht's backing rather than being essential to solving all the problems.<br /> <br /> That said, in agreement with Dwight, Evan is like most of the WoD canon NPCs in being setting straining special snowflake concepts with lots of plot armor that end up making them disappointing more often than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:20:45-07:00","id":938632,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mary Sue&quot; &quot;Special Snowflake&quot; can be hard to tell apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Plot Armor?&quot; if I may ask.<br /> <br /> <br /> you mean things designed to side track them from the way their designed being shielded against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T01:32:10-07:00","id":938681,"title":"","content":"Mary Sue, esp. in reference to the original fan-fic character, can do no wrong. The defining characteristics of her (and why she become a trope) were:<br /> <br /> 1) Everyone reacted positively to her regardless of what she did. Insult a Klingon's honor? Nobody treats her like a suicidal moron asking for a death match, and instead everyone (including Klingons) think it's a sign that she's brave and courageous for standing up to a big bad warrior. Break a couple up to steal the man? The jilted woman will be easily convinced to be happy for her ex and Mary, as they're clearly better together. Violate the Prime Directive more than Kirk, Picard, and Janeway combined? That's cool, every time was 10 times a better excuse then any of them ever had anyway.<br /> <br /> 2) Mary always gets the credit regardless of actual contribution, or even if she really caused the problem in the first place and everyone else is just cleaning up her mess (heavily reinforced by #1). Insulting a Klingon, which somehow ingratiates her with that Klingon, gets the crew wrapped up in a Klingon/Romulan battle. Mary gets the credit for leading to further bonds between the Federation and Klingon Empire in the defeat of a Romulan plot even though she spent the whole battle in the arboretum making sure some rare flower wasn't damaged while the rest of the crew was essential in a pitched space battle.<br /> <br /> Special snowflakes are characters that stack on things that are supposed to be rare to the point where it strains the rest of the group's fun. You're not just a Silver Fang and have royal blood, you're a PB 5 Silver Fang that's somehow in the direct line of succession for two different real world monarchies, and you have a five dot Numen spirit that's an avatar of Falcon that's constantly affirming you as the epitome of Silver Fangs is going overboard with it (at least for me).<br /> <br /> The line between the is really concept vs. execution. A special snowflake is a problem on a conceptual level. My example above could get played as a Mary Sue, or every non-Silver Fang in the game could find them so obnoxious - also screw Falcon's elitism - and end up the least popular Garou in the Caern as the Shadow Lords and Bone Gnawers unite in making sure they're a constant laughing stock for being so arrogant and presumptuous.<br /> <br /> Plot Armor is based on the narrative necessity that you know something isn't a real threat because the character is definitely going to survive. The plot demands that Frodo makes it to Mount Doom, so the trilogy of LotR never really makes it feel like Frodo is in any real danger for 95% of the books because he's destined to get to the end. This is acceptable if done well and all the reasons/ways Frodo escapes/survives make sense. It becomes a problem in the form of plot armor when the character just gets out of things. When plot armor is invoked with things like deus ex machina events, it hurts the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T05:22:16-07:00","id":938749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938598-evan-heals-the-past-a-mary-sue#post938598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">freak accident (a rape over a century ago)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if one can call that accident, but is that written? I can't remember any explicit statement on how his Wendigo ancestry came to be.<br /> <br /> That said, Evan is I think like any other lost cub someone who has to be educated in the ways of his tribe to be able to enter the tribe. That his potential teachers are reluctant (at the least) to accept his claims certainly doesn't help. But I think he has a kind of plot armour, in form of the ancestor spirits that guide him and help him overcome the obstacles in his way to a more widespread acceptance in the tribe.<br /> But to be a Mary Sue like character, I'd guess there would have to be more Evan centric material, where he can show such attributes. In the few material I read he was a minor character.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course I kind of dislike him for being a kind of signature character for a tribe, but not being stereotypical for that tribe. But North Wind's Fist isn't either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T06:22:20-07:00","id":938778,"title":"","content":"Evan is, at least, uncomfortably in the white saviour trope. You know, guy is white and yet -he- is the one solving all the POCs problems. Not a very good thing.<br /> <br /> Though, honestly, Evan actually does very little. Unlike Mari or Albercht, Evan tends to just sit there in the background and break up their fights. Or be the newbie. And by the time the revised TBs rolled out, people had figured out how problematic Evan was and so the Wendigo novel was about John NorthWind's Son.<br /> <br /> Do I think Evan is a Mary Sue or Special SnowFlake? He might be a bit snowflakey, but he does very little and only true deed he ever does in the novels is make up for his ancestors' crimes by dying (Time of Judgement novel 2).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T13:03:21-07:00","id":939726,"title":"","content":"oh on that fanfic is their a gramatical term for the line mentioning &quot;Youthful beauty and beautiful youth&quot;?<br /> <br /> wondered that a while...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T18:14:59-07:00","id":939883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/938598-evan-heals-the-past-a-mary-sue?p=939726#post939726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh on that fanfic is their a gramatical term for the line mentioning &quot;Youthful beauty and beautiful youth&quot;?<br /> <br /> wondered that a while...</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on what you call fanfic. It's called chiasmus, and it's been done at least since the Illiad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}